The attached image illustrates that Nano-11 induces a transient inflammatory response at the injection site and is internalized by recruited cells. Panel A quantifies various inflammatory cell types over time, showing a peak in Mac-2+ macrophages, Ly6C+ monocytes, antigen presenting cells, and eosinophils around day 2, while neutrophils decline rapidly after 6 hours. Panel B, using confocal microscopy, visually confirms the uptake of Nano-11 (red) by MHCII+ antigen-presenting cells, Ly6C+ monocytes, and Mac-2+ macrophages (green) at the injection site across different time points, indicating efficient delivery and cellular interaction.